          "text": "# Streaming Probe\n\n1. Always record the date and time of each observation immediately.\n2. Use descriptive adjectives to capture the sensory details of the environment.\n3. Avoid interpreting data in the moment to prevent observer bias.\n4. Write in complete sentences to ensure clarity for future analysis.\n5. Note the exact location of the subject using specific landmarks.\n6. Document the weather conditions as they may influence behavior.\n7. Use a consistent shorthand that is defined in a separate key.\n8. Record verbatim quotes whenever possible to preserve original meaning.\n9. Describe the physical layout of the space before detailing interactions.\n10. Maintain a neutral tone throughout the descriptive process.\n11. Note any interruptions or changes in the observation setting.\n12. Distinguish clearly between observed facts and personal reflections.\n13. Use a durable notebook to protect notes from environmental damage.\n14. Organize entries chronologically to maintain a clear timeline of events.\n15. Review and expand upon shorthand notes shortly after the session ends.\n16. Ensure that all handwriting is legible for external reviewers.",
